(BUF-34: format-string sources are supported for `set`, `is`, `append`, and `copy` when destination is a buffer.)
(expected output:
tag7
set7
app7
cp7
)
a number called n is 7.
a buffer called viadecl is "tag{n}".
print viadecl.
a buffer called viaset is 32 bytes in size.
set viaset to "set{n}".
print viaset.
a buffer called viaappend is 32 bytes in size.
append "app{n}" to viaappend.
print viaappend.
a buffer called viacopy is 32 bytes in size.
copy "cp{n}" to viacopy.
print viacopy.
